// CONTROL, not a claim — run by ../run.sh, expected to be REFUTED.
//
// A compilation query has the shape `source::psc <= target::<ordering>*`, and
// it is only worth anything if the target's ordering relation is not so coarse
// that it contains everything. kat/power-weak.kat is: its ar carries
// `eco*;po?;eco*`, eco* contains the identity, so ar contains po and every
// query against it passes for free (see ../open/compilation-IMM-vs-POWER.kat).
// This control makes sure the same never quietly happens to a target the suite
// does treat as a proof. If it starts holding, every compilation query against
// ARMv8 has become vacuous.
include "../../kat/arm8.kat"

assert po <= arm8::ob+
